List files in a hosted agent session.

Lists files and directories at the specified path in the session's filesystem.
When no path is provided, lists the root directory.

Agent details are automatically resolved from the azd environment. To read from
a deployed hosted agent without an azd project, supply --agent-endpoint, or
--project-endpoint with the deployed agent name in --agent-name, together with
--session-id. Direct mode does not read or save local session state.

Usage
  azd ai agent files list [remote-path] [flags]

Aliases
  list, ls

Flags
      --agent-endpoint string   : Full protocol endpoint URL of a deployed agent (no azd project required)
  -n, --agent-name string       : Agent name: the azure.yaml service name, or the deployed agent name with --project-endpoint
      --project-endpoint string : Foundry project endpoint URL; requires the deployed agent name via --agent-name (no azd project required)
  -s, --session-id string       : Session ID override (defaults to last invoke session; required with --agent-endpoint or --project-endpoint)
      --user-identity string    : User identity header value (sent as x-agent-user-id for local invocations and x-ms-user-identity for remote requests)

Global Flags
  -C, --cwd string         : Sets the current working directory
      --debug              : Enables debug and diagnostics logging
  -e, --environment string : The name of the environment to use
  -h, --help               : help for list
      --no-prompt          : Runs without prompts. Uses existing values; fails if any required value or decision cannot be resolved automatically.
  -o, --output string      : The output format (supported: json, table) (default "json")

Examples
  List files in the root directory (agent auto-detected)
    azd ai agent files list

  List files in a specific directory
    azd ai agent files list /data

  List files in table format
    azd ai agent files list /data --output table

  List with explicit session
    azd ai agent files list --session-id <session-id>

  List files of a deployed agent without an azd project
    azd ai agent files list /data --agent-name support --session-id <session-id> --no-prompt \
      --project-endpoint https://<account>.services.ai.azure.com/api/projects/<project>

  List files using the agent's protocol endpoint URL
    azd ai agent files list /data --session-id <session-id> --agent-endpoint \
      "https://<account>.services.ai.azure.com/api/projects/<project>/agents/support/endpoint/protocols/invocations"
